From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] user32, win32u: SetSystemCursor and SPI_SETCURSORS (3755)

SetSystemCursor was a stub that returned TRUE. It now replaces the system cursor
for the session: the cursor the process has loaded changes in place (windows
using the system cursor show the new image), processes started later load the
replacement, the given cursor is destroyed, and SystemParametersInfo
(SPI_SETCURSORS) puts the defaults back. CORE review (patches/notes/3755.txt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
